  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2023-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\((y-x)^2=4y^2\\) we get \\(y-x=\\pm 2y.\\) The choice \\(y-x=2y\\) gives \\(x=-y\\lt 0,\\) impossible, so \\(y-x=-2y,\\) meaning \\(x=3y.\\)\n\nSubstituting into \\(y^3=x^2=9y^2\\) gives \\(y=9,\\) hence \\(x=27\\) and \\(x+y=36.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Taking square roots, \\(y-x=\\pm 2y\\)",
        "Positivity rules out one sign and forces \\(x=3y;\\) substitute into \\(y^3=x^2\\)"
      ],
